Q) Difference Between ThreadPool Executor and ForkJoinPool
ThreadPool Executor:- ThreadPoolExecutor is used when you have many independent tasks (consumeData, ProcessData, SaveDataInDB).
-> Tasks Dont Depend on Each Other.
Ex:-
ExecutorService executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(3);
executor.submit(() -> consumeData());
executor.submit(() -> processData());
executor.submit(() -> saveDataInDB());
