ForkJoinPool:- When 1 worker thread finishes its queue, it steals tasks from another thread worker.
-> ForkJoinPool uses a work-stealing algorithm to keep threads busy.
-> It is used when you have one huge task that can be recursively broken into smaller tasks for better CPU utilization.
-> suitable for divide-and-conquer algorithms.

