Q) Difference between G1 vs ZGC
G1 GC:-
-------
-> G1 stands for Garbage First.
-> It divides the heap into multiple regions instead of managing the heap as a single large space.
-> It prioritizes collecting regions that contains the most garbage first.
-> Stops Application Threads while performing G1 GC but for a Very Minimal ms time.
-> Suitable for most enterprise applications.
Ex:-
----
Application Running -> Pause (GC) -> Application Running -> Pause (GC)

ZGC:-
-----
-> ZGC is an ultra-low latency garbage collector.
-> Most garbage collection work is performed concurrently while the application continues running.
-> Pause times typically remain in the sub-millisecond to a few milliseconds range, even with very large heap sizes.
-> Designed for applications where response time is critical. Application Running + GC Running

