Q) When a stale-version conflict occurred through optimistic locking, How retry should fetch latest version before Re-Attempting
A) When a stale-version conflict occurred, we caught the optimistic locking exception, rolled back that transaction, re-fetched the latest record, applied the required business update again, and retried the transaction.
-> We just dont catch the exception and retry, because if we retry, then we will retry with same old stale object which is of now use.
-> So, After caught the Exception, Before Re-Attempting, better rollback the Transaction, refetch the Latest record and retry the operation in a new Transaction.

