Q) What is @BatchSize
A) @BatchSize reduces the N+1 problem by grouping multiple lazy loads into batches using an IN clause, reducing number of database round trips.
Example:- 
---------
@BatchSize(size = 10)
@ManyToOne(fetch = FetchType.LAZY)
private Address address;

-> While Loading Employees only using findAll() Query, Hibernate knows Associated Address ID's.
-> Since, Address is LAZY, Hibernate does not immediately execute: "SELECT * FROM address ..."
-> When Lazy Address needs to be loaded, @Batch allows hibernate to batch them using in clause with Address ID's.
Example:- SELECT * FROM address WHERE id IN (A1, A2, A3, ..., A10);
-> If Employee Count is 3, then In Clause uses only 3 Address Id's though Batch size is 10.
-> @BatchSize(size = 10) means up to 10, not necessarily exactly 10.

