Q) How PESSIMISTIC_READ Works
A) When we use "PESSIMISTIC_READ" on "findById()" JPA Query, T1 acquires the Lock on Row-1.
-> Now T1 holds the Lock on Row-1. Other Threads like T2 Cannot perform any Update Operation on Row-1.
-> Lock is tied to T1's database transaction, not simply to the findById() method.
-> T1 Only Releases the Lock When the Transaction is Completed.
-> By This, Read safely; block conflicting writes

@Lock(LockModeType.PESSIMISTIC_READ)
Optional<Employee> findById(Long id);
