Q) What is PESSIMISTIC_WRITE
A) We use PESSIMISTIC_WRITE to perform flow read → lock → modify → save/commit.
-> You acquire the pessimistic write lock when fetching the row like findById().
-> You don't normally put PESSIMISTIC_WRITE specifically on save().
-> Purpose of PESSIMISTIC_WRITE is T2 transaction cannot modify that same row while T1 is working with it.
-> Read + prepare to modify; block other reads/writes as required by DB

Example:-
---------
@Lock(LockModeType.PESSIMISTIC_WRITE)
Employee findEmployeeById(Long id);

@Transactional
public void updateSalary(Long id) {

    Employee emp = repository.findEmployeeById(id); // lock
