Q) What are the different transaction propagation types in Spring ?
A) Propagation level defines:- What should happen when one transactional method calls another transactional method?

Transaction Propagation Types
------------------------------
REQUIRED:- Use existing transaction; if none exists, create one 
REQUIRES_NEW:-Always create a new transaction; suspend existing one 
SUPPORTS:- Use existing transaction if available; otherwise execute without one 
NOT_SUPPORTED:- Always execute without a transaction; suspend existing one 
MANDATORY:- Must have an existing transaction; otherwise exception 
NEVER:- Must NOT have a transaction; otherwise exception 
NESTED:- Execute within nested transaction/savepoint if supported

