Q) Serial GC vs Parallel GC
Serial GC:-
------------
-> Uses a single thread for Garbage Collection.
-> When GC runs, application threads are paused (Stop-The-World).
-> Simple and has low memory/CPU overhead.
-> Suitable for small applications / small heaps where long GC pauses are acceptable.

Parallel GC:-
-------------
-> Uses multiple threads for Garbage Collection.
-> JVM decides and provides the appropriate number of GC threads based on available CPUs and JVM settings.
-> Application threads are still paused during major GC work.
-> Multiple GC threads clean memory in parallel, so GC usually finishes faster than Serial GC.
-> Suitable for multi-core systems where throughput is more important than very low pause times.

