Q) How the main thread and child thread work when the child thread gets an exception in a multithreaded application ?
A) By default, a child thread's exception does not affect the main thread.
-> An uncaught exception in a child thread only terminates that thread.
-> It does not automatically propagate to the main thread.
-> It does not terminate the entire application unless it is the only running non-daemon thread.
-> Other threads continue to execute independently.

