Q) DB Connection Pool in Spring Boot and What is HikariCP ?
A) A database connection pool is a group of database connections that an application reuses.
-> These DB Pool Connections can be reused when the application needs to communicate to the DB.
-> Instead of creating and closing a brand-new connection for every single query, application borrows an active connection from pool, runs query, and instantly returns.
Example:- Request → Borrow Connection from Pool → Query → Return Connection to Pool
-> After queries complete, connections return to the pool so that New requests can reuse those same connections.
-> The Default Connection Pool is HikariCP.

What is HikariCP
-----------------
-> HikariCP is a high-performance JDBC connection pool library.
-> It is the default connection pool in Spring Boot when using spring-boot-starter-data-jpa.
-> Spring Boot automatically creates and manages a HikariDataSource if database properties are configured.

Important HikariCP Properties
------------------------------
spring.datasource.url=jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/machinedb
spring.datasource.username=machine_user
spring.datasource.password=password

spring.datasource.hikari.maximum-pool-size=10         // Maximum number of DB connections Machine MS can use at once.
spring.datasource.hikari.minimum-idle=2               // Keeps at least 2 idle connections ready.
spring.datasource.hikari.connection-timeout=30000     // Wait up to 30 seconds for a free connection. After that, HikariCP throws an exception.
spring.datasource.hikari.idle-timeout=600000          // Closes connections that remain idle for 10 minutes.
spring.datasource.hikari.max-lifetime=1800000         // Replaces connections after 30 minutes to avoid stale or database-closed connections.

Note:- If there are 5 instance of Machines-MS and each has configured maximum-pool-size=10, then (5 instances × 10 connections) = 50 DB connections will be created.

