Q) What is Virtual Threads
-> Traditional Platform Threads creates large number of expensive OS threads.
-> Traditional platform threads are relatively costly in memory and system resources.
-> If thousands of requests are waiting on HTTP calls, database calls, or file I/O, thousands of platform threads can become expensive.
-> Thread pool can become exhausted if we create costly platform threads to execute 1000 HTTP Requests.


-> Virtual threads are lightweight threads managed by the JVM.
-> Handle high concurrency: Thousands or millions of concurrent requests can be supported more easily.
-> Improve blocking I/O scalability: A virtual thread waiting for DB or HTTP response usually frees the underlying platform thread to do other work.
-> Reduce thread-pool tuning: Instead of carefully limiting request threads for I/O-heavy workloads, applications can often use one virtual thread per task/request.

