Q) If your application receives huge traffic, how will you handle it ?
A) Below are the Steps we can handle huge traffic.

1) Load Balancer:- Distribute incoming requests across multiple instances. Example: Nginx, AWS ALB.
2) Horizontal Scaling:- Run multiple Spring Boot instances. Use Kubernetes/Auto Scaling Groups.
3) Caching:- Use Redis for frequently accessed data. Reduce database hits.
4) Database Optimization:- Create proper indexes. Use connection pooling (HikariCP).
5) Asynchronous Processing:- Use Kafka/RabbitMQ for Asynchronous operations. Process tasks in the background.
6) Rate Limiting:- Prevent abuse and traffic spikes. Example: API Gateway, Resilience4j.
7) Retry + Circuit Breaker:- Handle temporary downstream failures. Use Resilience4j.

