Q) Difference Between RestTemplate and OpenFeignClient
RestTemplate
-------------
-> It is an imperative, older and in Maintenance Mode.
-> It requires more boilerplate code like "restTemplate.exchange(url, HttpMethod.GET, null, Employee.class);"
-> We Manually Manage Urls's
Example:-
----------
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/users")
public class UserController {

private final RestTemplate restTemplate;

@GetMapping("/{id}")
    public String getUser(@PathVariable Long id) {
        return restTemplate.getForObject("http://user-service/api/users/" + id, String.class);
    }
}


OpenFeignClient
---------------
-> OpenFeign is Cleaner and declarative.
-> It defines an interface, no manual URL building or request code.
-> Less boilerplate and easier to read/maintain.
-> Supports integrations such as load balancing, retries, and interceptors more easily in Spring Cloud.

Example:-
---------
@FeignClient(name = "user-service", url = "http://user-service")
public interface UserClient {

    @GetMapping("/api/users/{id}")
    String getUser(@PathVariable Long id);
}

Invoke From Rest Controller
---------------------------
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/users")
@AllArgsConstructor
public class UserController {

private final UserClient userClient;

  @GetMapping("/{id}")
    public String getUser(@PathVariable Long id) {
        return userClient.getUser(id);
    }
}

